{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1000", "sample_idx": 2, "model_name": "google/gemma-3n-e2b-it", "content": "Raymond III Count of Tripoli was a powerful ruler who reigned from 1146 to 1199. He was the son of Raymond I Count of Tripoli and a significant figure in the Crusades and the history of the Levant. His reign saw both expansion and conflict for the County of Tripoli a strategically important territory in the Eastern Mediterranean.\n\n*Early Life and Ascendancy* Raymond III inherited the County of Tripoli at a young age following the death of his father. He faced immediate challenges consolidating power and defending the county from internal opposition and external threats. His early reign was marked by successful military campaigns against Muslim forces particularly those of the Ayyubid dynasty. He skillfully navigated the complex political landscape of the Crusader states forging alliances with other rulers and engaging in diplomatic maneuvering to protect Tripoli's interests. He also focused on strengthening the county's defenses and infrastructure.\n\nRaymond III's reign was characterized by significant military achievements. He expanded Tripoli's territory through successful campaigns against the Ayyubids and other Muslim powers. He established a strong military force and implemented effective military strategies. His military victories secured Tripoli's borders and ensured its continued independence. He also engaged in numerous skirmishes and battles with various adversaries maintaining a precarious balance of power.\n\n*Diplomacy and Foreign Policy* Raymond III was a shrewd diplomat adept at forging alliances and navigating complex international relations. He maintained close ties with the other Crusader states particularly those in the Levant. He sought to secure support from European powers including France and England to defend Tripoli against Muslim aggression. He also engaged in diplomatic negotiations with Muslim rulers seeking to establish peaceful relations and secure trade agreements. His diplomatic efforts were instrumental in maintaining Tripoli's independence and prosperity. He was known for his skillful negotiation and ability to build coalitions.\n\n*Legacy and Decline* Raymond III's reign was a period of relative stability and prosperity for the County of Tripoli. He strengthened the county's defenses expanded its territory and secured its independence. However his reign also witnessed a gradual decline in Tripoli's power and influence. The increasing strength of the Ayyubid dynasty and the internal divisions within the Crusader states eventually led to Tripoli's vulnerability. After his death the county faced increasing pressure from Muslim forces and ultimately lost much of its territory. Raymond III's legacy is one of a successful ruler who defended Tripoli against overwhelming odds and left a lasting mark on the history of the Levant. His military prowess diplomatic skills and strategic vision secured Tripoli's survival for a considerable period.\n\n\n\n", "logprobs": [{"token": "Raymond", "logprob": -0.1434636116027832}, {"token": "▁III", "logprob": -1.6689286894688848e-06}, {"token": "▁Count", "logprob": -6.854299135738984e-05}, {"token": "▁of", "logprob": -2.50339189733495e-06}, {"token": "▁Tripoli", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "▁was", "logprob": -0.0874934121966362}, {"token": "▁a", "logprob": -0.029306435957551003}, {"token": "▁powerful", "logprob": -0.5966804027557373}, {"token": "▁ruler", "logprob": -0.5979602336883545}, {"token": "▁who", "logprob": -0.6220458745956421}, {"token": "▁reigned", "logprob": -0.5052332282066345}, {"token": "▁from", "logprob": -1.148343563079834}, {"token": "▁", "logprob": -0.002159527037292719}, {"token": "1", "logprob": -0.00012742661056108773}, {"token": "1", "logprob": -0.0009628665866330266}, {"token": "4", "logprob": -0.6788371801376343}, {"token": "6", "logprob": -1.3646454811096191}, {"token": "▁to", "logprob": -0.018537255004048347}, {"token": "▁", "l